=== P3 Dashboard widget 0110 VehicleUpgradesWidget (Android) ===
Capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3, Kotlin (repo pins 2.x; prompt floor 2.2.x) -- AVAILABLE
  (JDK 21 JetBrains JBR at %JAVA_HOME%, Android SDK at %LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk, gradlew 8.14.5).
  :android:assembleRelease produces a Release APK (gate below), so the platform capability is present --
  this gate is NOT a platform-capability block. NOTE: the Gradle module path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts
  include(":android"); projectDir = app/), so the prompt gate's ':app:'/'ktlintCheck'/'detekt' are addressed as
  ':android:assembleRelease', ':android:testReleaseUnitTest', ':android:ktlintCheck', ':android:detekt'. The
  unit-test scope is artifact-isolated to '*vehicleupgrades*' (the shared androidTest source set is not
  host-run; no emulator), matching the P3/0097 Subscriptions precedent.

P3 core prerequisites reused: A1 theme/tokens (TeslaTokens/Spacing), shared component library
  (ui: Badge/BodyText/Caption/Icon/IconButton/MetricValue/MetricLabel/PanelTitle; feedback:
  EmptyState/ErrorDisplay/Skeleton/FeedbackGlyphs; datadisplay: DataFreshness/DataDisplayGlyphs; motion: FadeIn),
  S7/S8 data layer (VehiclesRepository/VehiclesStore -> vehicles + vehicleUpgrades; DrivingRepository/DrivingStore
  -> drives; SharingRepository/SharingStore -> shareLinks), S10 i18n catalog, S11 diagnostics Logger
  (view.opened), S8 BaseFeedViewModel/UiState/Resource cache-then-network contract.

Web source: web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/VehicleUpgradesWidget.tsx (THE spec). Native output:
  apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/VehicleUpgradesWidget/
    VehicleUpgradesModel.kt             (pure asString/isEligible/parseUpgrades/daysUntil/parseDateMillis/
                                         formatExpiryDate/activeShareLinks/nearestExpiry + projection +
                                         registration; no Compose/Android/HTTP)
    VehicleUpgradesSource.kt            (data port + S7 repo / S8 store adapters + upgrades-primary three-feed
                                         composition: vehicleUpgradesResource + mergeUpgrades + drives->shareLinks chain)
    VehicleUpgradesWidgetViewModel.kt   (resolves first vehicle -> upgrades(+drives->shareLinks) onto UiState)
    VehicleUpgradesWidget.kt            (Compose: WidgetShell-equiv header + compact count tile + standard
                                         upgrades list + share-links section; ArrowUpCircle/Link2 glyphs; previews)
Tests: src/test/.../vehicleupgrades/{VehicleUpgradesProjectionTest(17), VehicleUpgradesWidgetViewModelTest(12),
       VehicleUpgradesSourceTest(11)}; src/androidTest/.../vehicleupgrades/VehicleUpgradesWidgetUiTest(7).

Parity (web -> native):
  - Registry: id 'vehicle-upgrades', category 'vehicle', default 2x4, min 1x2, max 4x40 (VehicleUpgradesRegistration).
  - States: loading skeleton; hard error + retry (ONLY when the per-vehicle UPGRADES feed errors w/ no cache, web
    isError from useVehicleUpgrades); content; empty (no upgrades AND no share links => friendly inline empties
    "All upgrades applied" + "No active share links"); stale/offline cached + freshness chip + auto-refresh; a
    vehicles-list error degrades to a cached empty (web disables the upgrades query when no id resolves).
  - Upgrades-primary contract: shellProps loading/updatedAt/isFetching/isStale/isError/onRefresh all flow from
    useVehicleUpgrades; the useDrives -> useShareLinks chain only enriches the share-links section and never gates
    the surface (verified: upgradesAreContentEvenWhileDrivesNeverResolve).
  - Compact (size.cols<=1): ArrowUpCircle glyph + eligible-upgrade count + "available", else "Up to date" badge.
  - Standard (>1 col): title "Upgrades & Sharing" + ArrowUpCircle; available-upgrades list (name; $price chip;
    optional description; eligibility caption when isWide (cols>=3); Eligible/Not-eligible badge) or the centered
    "All upgrades applied" row; divider; share-links section (Active links count + Nearest expiry warning chip) or
    the "No active share links" empty state.
  - parseUpgrades: data.upgrades array (name<-name/title, price<-price/cost, description<-description/summary,
    eligible = value !== false) else top-level object keys; asString / isEligible coercions reproduced.
  - daysUntil = Math.ceil((expiry-now)/86400000); activeShareLinks (no-expiry/future/unparseable kept, past
    dropped); nearestExpiry = soonest future-dated active link; fmtDate -> MMM d, yyyy else em-dash.
  - i18n: 11 chrome keys resolve from S10 (translation_widget_upgrades_{title,available,upToDate,upgradesHeading,
    eligible,notEligible,allApplied,shareLinksHeading,activeLinks,nearestExpiry,noShareLinks}); already shipped in
    res/values/strings.xml, so no catalog edit. The web's hardcoded 'Unknown Upgrade' parse fallback (not a t()
    call on web) stays a model default.
  - a11y: refresh IconButton labelled; each upgrade row, the compact hero, and each share-links summary row fold
    into one TalkBack phrase; section headings marked heading().
  - Telemetry: view.opened emitted once with surface slug 'VehicleUpgradesWidget' (P1/S11), carrying no payload.

